---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import NewsletterEmbed from '../../components/NewsletterEmbed.astro';

const articleStyles = `
    .tip {
        padding: 14px 0;
        margin-bottom: 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .tip:last-child {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
        margin-bottom: 0;
        padding-bottom: 14px;
    }
    .tip-number {
        font-size: 0.65rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
        margin-bottom: 1px;
    }
    .tip h2 {
        font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        line-height: 1.3;
        margin-bottom: 4px;
        letter-spacing: 0;
        color: var(--text);
    }
    .tip p {
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin-bottom: 3px;
    }
    .tip-ref {
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        color: #0066cc;
        text-decoration: none;
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 3px;
    }
    .tip-ref:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
    .section-heading {
        font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
        font-size: 0.68rem;
        font-weight: 500;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
        margin-top: 40px;
        margin-bottom: 2px;
        padding-top: 0;
        border-top: none;
    }
`;
---
<ArticleLayout
    title="31 science-backed tips to fix low testosterone — Max Guerois"
    description="Nothing besides TRT/steroids will drastically increase levels. The key is lifestyle changes. Here are 31 science-backed tips. By Max Guerois."
    ogUrl="https://maxguerois.com/experiments/testosterone"
    ogImage="https://maxguerois.com/health-journey/og/zeromeetup-157.jpg"
    articleStyles={articleStyles}
>

<div class="container">
    <a href="/newsletter" class="back">← Back to the newsletter</a>

    <div class="article-meta">Male Protocol · March 2026</div>
    <h1 class="article-title">If you want to fix low testosterone, here are 31 science-backed tips you could come up with</h1>

    <div class="tldr">
        <div class="tldr-label">TL;DR</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Nothing besides TRT/steroids will drastically increase levels.</li>
            <li>Don't fall for fancy supplement labels.</li>
            <li>The key is lifestyle changes, with some supplements as support.</li>
            <li>Morning and evening rituals matter — timing your supplements correctly is half the work.</li>
            <li>Sleep, diet, stress, and training compound over time. There are no shortcuts.</li>
            <li>Low testosterone hits energy, muscle, mood, and libido — all at once.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="article-body">

        <p>My male friends keep asking me the same question: how do you boost testosterone naturally? I've been asked enough times that I finally decided to write it all down properly.</p>

        <p>I've seen countless posts/advice on boosting testosterone. Let's be real — nothing besides TRT/steroids will drastically increase levels. Don't fall for fancy supplement labels. The key is lifestyle changes, with some supplements as support.</p>

        <p>And it actually matters. Low testosterone means low energy, reduced muscle mass, higher body fat, brain fog, low libido, and mood swings. It's a slow decline — and most guys don't even notice it's happening.</p>

        <p>This is what you can do. This is backed by science.</p>

        <!-- MORNING RITUAL -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Morning Ritual</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">01</div>
            <h2>Vitamin D3</h2>
            <p>Supports hormone function and bone health. Research has shown that Vitamin D3 supplementation can improve testosterone levels in men with low Vitamin D status.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Pilz+vitamin+D+testosterone+2011" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pilz, S., et al. (2011) ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">02</div>
            <h2>Tongkat Ali</h2>
            <p>Known for boosting libido and testosterone levels. Studies show it may improve libido and have an effect on testosterone.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Tambi+Tongkat+Ali+testosterone+2012" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tambi, M. I. B. M., et al. (2012) ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">03</div>
            <h2>B-Vitamin Complex</h2>
            <p>Essential for energy metabolism and overall health. B-vitamins play a role in energy metabolism, with B6 and B12 supporting nervous system function.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">04</div>
            <h2>Boron</h2>
            <p>Trace mineral that influences testosterone levels. Some studies suggest boron supplementation can increase testosterone.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Naghii+boron+testosterone+2011" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Naghii, M. R., et al. (2011) ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">05</div>
            <h2>Maca Root</h2>
            <p>Adaptogen known for enhancing energy, stamina, and libido (<em>not testosterone</em>). Research indicates it doesn't significantly impact testosterone levels.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Gonzales+maca+root+libido+2002" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gonzales, G. F., et al. (2002) ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">06</div>
            <h2>Creatine</h2>
            <p>Supports muscle growth and strength and may influence testosterone levels. Studies link creatine supplementation with increased muscle mass and slight test increases.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Volek+creatine+testosterone+1997" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Volek, J. S., et al. (1997) ↗</a>
        </div>

        <!-- EVENING RITUAL -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Evening Ritual — 60 min before sleep</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">07</div>
            <h2>Zinc</h2>
            <p>Essential for testosterone production and immune function. Studies indicate zinc supplementation can increase testosterone.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Prasad+zinc+testosterone+1996" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prasad et al., 1996 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">08</div>
            <h2>Magnesium (Citrate or Glycinate)</h2>
            <p>Supports muscle and nerve function; aids relaxation and sleep. Magnesium has positive effects on muscle, nerve function, and sleep.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Cao+magnesium+sleep+2009" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cao et al., 2009 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">09</div>
            <h2>Omega-3 Fatty Acids</h2>
            <p>Anti-inflammatory effects + supports good sleep. Research suggests Omega-3s support sleep.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Hansen+omega+3+sleep+2014" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hansen et al., 2014 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <!-- ADJUSTMENTS -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Adjustments</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">10</div>
            <h2>Remove Sugar and Processed Foods</h2>
            <p>Sugar intake disrupts hormonal balance. A study linked high sugar intake to lower testosterone.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Maggio+sugar+testosterone+2013" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maggio et al., 2013 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">11</div>
            <h2>Remove Seed Oils</h2>
            <p>Use butter or extra virgin olive oil. Trans fats from seed oils negatively impact health.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Mozaffarian+trans+fat+cardiovascular+2006" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mozaffarian et al., 2006 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">12</div>
            <h2>Say No to Alcohol</h2>
            <p>Excessive alcohol lowers testosterone.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Emanuele+alcohol+testosterone+1998" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Emanuele &amp; Emanuele, 1998 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">13</div>
            <h2>Adios Tobacco and Drugs</h2>
            <p>These destroy overall health and hormone levels, including vaping.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">14</div>
            <h2>Hydration</h2>
            <p>Drink plenty of water throughout the day. Aim for 2 liters.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">15</div>
            <h2>Test Diet</h2>
            <p>Focus on whole foods like eggs, red meat, butter, fruits, and vegetables. A diet rich in protein aids muscle building and weight loss, which support higher testosterone levels. Aim for 2x body weight in grams (e.g., 80kg = 160g protein).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">16</div>
            <h2>Raw or Fat Natural Milk &amp; Coconut Water</h2>
            <p>Highly beneficial.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">17</div>
            <h2>Coffee Intake</h2>
            <p>Limit to morning hours, but drink <strong>90 min after waking</strong> to avoid disrupting sleep.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- LIFESTYLE FIXES -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Lifestyle Fixes</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">18</div>
            <h2>Weight Lifting — 3-5 times a week</h2>
            <p>Boosts testosterone levels. Studies show resistance training enhances test production.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Ahtiainen+resistance+training+testosterone+2003" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ahtiainen et al., 2003 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">19</div>
            <h2>HIIT Training</h2>
            <p>Short, intense bursts of activity boost testosterone.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">20</div>
            <h2>Bedroom Activities (Morning)</h2>
            <p>Sexual activity (not self-induced) can influence testosterone levels.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=van+Anders+sexual+activity+testosterone+2011" target="_blank" rel="noopener">van Anders et al., 2011 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">21</div>
            <h2>Regular Movement</h2>
            <p>Avoid sitting for prolonged periods — don't be lazy!</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">22</div>
            <h2>Outdoor Activities</h2>
            <p>Sunlight exposure is crucial for Vitamin D synthesis.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- SLEEP -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Sleep is Essential</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">23</div>
            <h2>Quality Sleep</h2>
            <p>Invest in a comfortable bed and pillow — maintain a regular sleep schedule. Sleep is crucial for hormone regulation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">24</div>
            <h2>Sleep Tracking</h2>
            <p>Monitor sleep patterns for improvement. Devices like the Ultrahuman Ring help.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- XENOESTROGENS -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Avoid Xenoestrogens &amp; Estrogen-Like Substances</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">25</div>
            <h2>Personal Care &amp; Household Products</h2>
            <p>Found in some plastics, shampoos, deodorants, and toothpaste — these disrupt hormonal balance.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Darbre+parabens+endocrine+2006" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Darbre, 2006 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <!-- STRESS MANAGEMENT -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Stress Management</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">26</div>
            <h2>Cold Showers</h2>
            <p>Finish each shower with 30–60 seconds of cold water. Be a man. Get used to it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">27</div>
            <h2>Ice Baths — 2-4 times a week</h2>
            <p>Boost resilience, recovery, general health, burns fat + boosts test. Cold exposure activates brown adipose tissue (BAT), which burns calories.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=van+der+Lans+cold+brown+adipose+tissue+2013" target="_blank" rel="noopener">van der Lans et al., 2013 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">28</div>
            <h2>Mindfulness &amp; Relaxation</h2>
            <p>Meditation helps manage stress by lowering cortisol, which destroys testosterone. If meditation isn't for you, go for walks in nature.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- FASTING -->
        <h2 class="section-heading">Fasting</h2>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">29</div>
            <h2>Fasting Once a Week (24h) or Every Two Weeks (36h)</h2>
            <p>Research suggests fasting has various health benefits, including potential testosterone impacts.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">30</div>
            <h2>Short-Term Fasting</h2>
            <p>Increases LH (hormone stimulating testosterone production).</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Anderson+fasting+luteinizing+hormone+testosterone+1987" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anderson et al., 1987 ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="tip">
            <div class="tip-number">31</div>
            <h2>Weight Loss &amp; Testosterone</h2>
            <p>Fasting can lead to reduced body fat, which indirectly raises test levels.</p>
            <a class="tip-ref" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=Ng+Tang+Fui+weight+loss+testosterone" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ng Tang Fui et al., 2017 ↗</a>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="article-footer">
        <span class="author-line">By <a href="/">Max Guerois</a></span>
    </div>

    <!-- Newsletter CTA -->
    <div style="margin-top: 48px;">
        <NewsletterEmbed />
    </div>
</div>
</ArticleLayout>
